{#
settings/_clock.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Twelve- or twenty-four-hour clock. Submits on change and redirects, like the
timezone picker beside it and for the same reason: the choice changes every
time printed anywhere on the page, not something local to this form.

The first option is not a blank entry — it is "follow your language", the state
a user who has never chosen is already in, and it stays that way rather than
being silently converted into whichever format it currently resolves to. See
ClockFormatResolver::chosen().

Each option carries a live sample of the current time in its own format, which
is the only thing that makes the choice self-explanatory: "12-hour" and
"24-hour" are the names of the thing, "2:30 pm" and "14:30" are the thing.

Variables:
  clockOptions  {value: sample} — the two real formats, rendered
  activeClock   string|null   the user's own choice, null when following
  defaultClock  string        the sample the language resolves to
  clockPlacements       list<ClockPlacement>  every place the running clock can go
  activeClockPlacement  ClockPlacement        the user's, the topbar when unset

The second picker is where the running clock is drawn. In this card rather than
one of its own because it is the same question from the other side: this card
says how a time is written, that one where the time now is written.
#}
{% import '_partials/_select.html.twig' as select %}
<div class="px-4 py-3">
    <form method="post" action="{{ path('app_settings_clock_update') }}" data-turbo="false" data-controller="ui--auto-submit">
        <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('settings-clock') }}">

        <label for="settings-clock" class="sr-only">{{ 'settings.clock.label'|trans }}</label>

        <select id="settings-clock"
                name="clock"
                data-action="change->ui--auto-submit#submit"
                {{ select.enhance() }}
                class="select-field w-full h-9 text-sm">
            <option value="" {{ activeClock is null ? 'selected' : '' }}>
                {{ 'settings.clock.follow_language'|trans({'%sample%': defaultClock}) }}
            </option>

            {% for value, sample in clockOptions %}
                <option value="{{ value }}" {{ value == activeClock ? 'selected' : '' }}>
                    {{ ('settings.clock.option.' ~ value)|trans({'%sample%': sample}) }}
                </option>
            {% endfor %}
        </select>
    </form>

    <form method="post" action="{{ path('app_settings_clock_placement') }}" data-turbo="false" data-controller="ui--auto-submit"
          class="mt-3">
        <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token('settings-clock') }}">

        <label for="settings-clock-placement" class="block mb-1.5 text-xs text-ink-muted">
            {{ 'settings.clock.placement.label'|trans }}
        </label>

        <select id="settings-clock-placement"
                name="placement"
                data-action="change->ui--auto-submit#submit"
                {{ select.enhance() }}
                class="select-field w-full h-9 text-sm">
            {% for placement in clockPlacements %}
                <option value="{{ placement.value }}" {{ placement == activeClockPlacement ? 'selected' : '' }}>
                    {{ placement.transKey|trans }}
                </option>
            {% endfor %}
        </select>
    </form>
</div>
